# GenAI Launchpad — Cursor Project Rules

## What This Project Is
An event-driven AI workflow platform. Clients POST events to a FastAPI endpoint;
a Celery worker picks them up asynchronously and runs them through a chain of Nodes.
Results are stored back to PostgreSQL. The stack is FastAPI + Celery + Redis + PostgreSQL + Pydantic-AI.

## Architecture at a Glance
```
POST /events/<workflow>
  → FastAPI validates schema → stores Event to DB → queues Celery task → 202 Accepted
  → Celery worker: fetches event → runs Workflow → stores TaskContext back to DB
  → Workflow: chains Nodes sequentially; Routers branch dynamically
```

## Key Directories
| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/api/` | FastAPI endpoints — one file per workflow |
| `app/schemas/` | Pydantic event schemas — validated on ingest |
| `app/workflows/` | Workflow classes + their node subdirectories |
| `app/core/nodes/` | Base classes: Node, AgentNode, BaseRouter, ConcurrentNode |
| `app/prompts/` | Jinja2 prompt templates (`.j2`) with YAML frontmatter |
| `app/services/` | Shared services (PromptManager, etc.) |
| `app/worker/` | Celery config and task definition |
| `app/database/` | SQLAlchemy models, session, repository |
| `docker/` | Docker Compose stack |
| `tests/` | Unit and integration tests |
| `docs/` | Architecture docs and workflow guides |

## How to Add a New Workflow (the core pattern)
1. `app/schemas/<name>_schema.py` — define `MyEventSchema(BaseModel)`
2. `app/workflows/<name>_workflow_nodes/` — one file per node
3. `app/workflows/<name>_workflow.py` — wire nodes into `WorkflowSchema`
4. `app/workflows/workflow_registry.py` — add `MY_WORKFLOW = MyWorkflow` to enum
5. `app/api/<name>_endpoint.py` — POST endpoint, mirrors `support_endpoint.py`
6. `app/api/router.py` — mount the new endpoint
7. `requests/events/<name>_event.json` — test payload
8. `app/prompts/<name>.j2` — prompt templates if using AgentNode

## Node Types
- **`Node`** — plain async node, pure Python logic
- **`AgentNode`** — LLM call via Pydantic-AI; implement `get_agent_config()` + `process()`
- **`BaseRouter`** — branches workflow; set `self.routes` + `self.fallback` in `__init__`
- **`ConcurrentNode`** — runs `concurrent_nodes` in parallel via `asyncio.gather`

## State Passing Between Nodes
```python
self.save_output(MyOutputModel(...))        # store in task_context.nodes["MyNode"]
self.get_output(OtherNode)                  # retrieve by class reference
```

## AgentNode Config
```python
def get_agent_config(self) -> AgentConfig:
    return AgentConfig(
        model_provider=ModelProvider.ANTHROPIC,
        model_name="claude-3-5-sonnet-latest",
        output_type=MyPydanticOutputModel,
        system_prompt=PromptManager.get_prompt("my_template"),
    )
```

## Code Conventions
- No comments unless the WHY is non-obvious
- All node outputs are Pydantic `BaseModel` subclasses
- Prompt templates: static content in system prompt, dynamic content in a separate user-turn template
- Never modify `app/core/` or `app/worker/tasks.py` — they are framework code
- LLM provider set via env vars (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, etc.) in `docker/.env`

## Running the Stack
```bash
make start       # start Docker stack
make stop        # stop Docker stack
make logs        # tail all logs
make test        # run test suite
make lint        # run ruff linter
make migrate     # apply DB migrations
```
